  "id": "COMPOUND:43014 - PROTEIN:6231",
  "verbalization": "Harmalacidine is shown to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is known to methylate histone H3 lysine 9 (H3K9). This interaction is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate that Harmalacidine targets the same complex and ultimately leads to the Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, H3 lysine-9 specific 5 enzyme. The evidence suggests that Harmalacidine acts as a modulator of the PRC2 complex, potentially inhibiting the methylation of H3K9, which is associated with gene repression. The consistent targeting of the same complex across different pathways strengthens the hypothesis that Harmalacidine exerts its effects through a mechanism involving the PRC2 complex and its downstream histone methyltransferase activity. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong and reliable relationship, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the specific mode of action and therapeutic potential.",
